          "id": "c0bc5cbd72c06f2d1dd627a72d1047dbeddb13ee",
          "message": "Fix flaky macOS test: concurrent search during updates overlaps by construction (#230)\n\nThe searcher only gets the lock between the writer's updates, so whether it\nfound the lock free 3 times in 40 rounds was up to the scheduler; on a macOS\nrunner it sometimes did not. The writer now waits for one more search a few\ntimes per round, so the overlap is made rather than hoped for. The checks are\nthe same.\n\nFixes #229\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017dmSnSHynuShB9XC8YFa7s",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-27T02:09:32Z",
          "tree_id": "9cacf224773c3fce76ae36fd44ed6c52cf21a50a",
