          "distinct": true,
          "id": "fd2a573aff4f8b0aa94c736b399c5b6330efcba6",
          "message": "C1 design: measured after C1.2, C1.3 re-scoped (#235)\n\nA one-file watcher update now costs the same at 302k files as at 6k\n(2.95 vs 2.8 ms), so C1.3's removal goal is met already. Under a heavy\nstream the lock-held work is building posting lists (76% roaring inserts)\nand searches wait for install steps by design of the lock protocol. C1.3\nbecomes \"build each batch's delta off the lock\".\n\nAccept-instructions: index_save\n\n#232 made the benchmark save a checkpointed index, as a server's later\nsaves are: +48.6% instructions, 29% less wall time. No product change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017dmSnSHynuShB9XC8YFa7s",
          "timestamp": "2026-10-27T04:40:27Z",
